sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant S as Scheduler (trades.reconcile, every 10 s)
    participant DB as Postgres
    participant X as Waxpeer

    S->>DB: read ≤ 100 oldest due orders (buying / trade_sent, next_check_at ≤ now) + their trade
    S->>DB: end the read transaction (no lock held across Waxpeer)
    S->>X: check-many-project-id [polled orders' ids]  (≤ 100 per call)
    alt lookup fails (unavailable, 429, 403, refusal)
        Note over S: nothing written — every row stays due for the next tick
    else answered
        loop each polled order (its own transaction; one failure never stops the tick)
            S->>DB: lock order, then trade (FOR UPDATE); re-check: still followed, not buy_pending, still due
            Note over S: ours = picked by the stored Waxpeer id; a 6 without a known id is NOT ours<br/>(maybe a refused attempt while our lost buy went through) → unseen
            alt several live trades, no Waxpeer id
                S->>DB: attention ambiguous_trade (once; no refund)
            else none of ours
                Note over S,DB: lost answer: buy_unconfirmed_at older than 10 min → attention buy_unconfirmed (once; no refund, R3)<br/>known Waxpeer id unseen for 10 min → attention ambiguous_trade (once)
            else our trade (live, or by its known id)
                S->>DB: clear an open buy_unconfirmed; mirror it, then apply the status
                Note over DB: 4 → trade_sent · 4 + release_date / 5 / released → delivered<br/>6 after acceptance / penalties → delivered, then attention rolled_back (money spent)<br/>6 otherwise → returned + refund to the balance (not_accepted)
            end
            S->>DB: next_check_at = now + 10 s; commit
        end
    end
    loop each due order still buy_pending
        S->>S: attempt_buy — takes the order's lease or does nothing (buy.mmd)
    end

    Note over S,X: trades.protection (hourly): delivered trades at 4 + release_date — 5 → released, 6 → attention rolled_back
    Note over S,X: trades.audit (23:30 UTC): settled trades of 14 days — a new divergence → audit_verdict + attention audit_divergence, once per verdict
    Note over S,DB: orders.expiry (every 60 s): pending past expires_at, no kassa-held attempt → cancelled (created attempts cancelled)
